    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for LawDog presents a clear hierarchy of upside, headlined by **Bryce Harper** (74.91) and **Lawrence Butler** (71.64). **Bryce Harper** is our must-start anchor, leveraging a soft matchup against Eric Lauer (5.41 xERA) and a massive 0.387 xwOBA advantage to drive the lineup\u2019s core ceiling. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** is a high-leverage play despite his projected #8 spot in the order; the combination of a favorable park and a significant +19% SP Skill boost against Merrill Kelly makes him the second-most valuable asset on the board. **Luis Arraez** also warrants mention as a high-floor play (66.78), benefiting from a strong +13% SP Skill advantage against Seth Lugo and the ideal #1 lineup slot to stabilize our AVG category.\n\nStrategic platoon and order adjustments proved pivotal today. **Jonathan Aranda** (63.20) saw his score swell behind a +12% dynamic platoon edge against the righty Braydon Fisher, effectively securing his spot in the 1B slot. On the bench, **Drew Gilbert** (50.48) was the most difficult exclusion, coming within a fraction of the starting threshold. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the higher overall efficiency of our starting OF unit and the specific situational boosts tied to our mid-order hitters, leaving **Drew Gilbert** as the odd man out. While **Gavin Sheets** sits on the bench with a 49.10 score, he carries a 35% rain risk, providing an easy justification for keeping him sidelined to protect our games-played cap. We remain alert for any updates to the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Gleyber Torres**, as their final batting positions may shift their efficiency scores before first pitch.",
